 175: | `public/js/suite/tracker-feed.js` | Still on disk but **unrouted** - `public/js/app.js:147` records its removal ("feeding consolidated to More grid"). Left untouched: modifying unreachable code adds risk with no behavioural gain. |
 176: | `public/js/tabs/feeding-tab.js` | Live and routed. Wired. |
 177: 
 178: So the live surfaces wired are **two**, not seven: `suite/roll-v2.js` (the sole player/ST roller) and
 179: `tabs/feeding-tab.js`. Line numbers in the Code Map are likewise stale throughout (e.g. the
 180: feeding-tab rote comparison the story calls `:976` is now `:1048`); the named call sites were located
 181: by shape, not by number.
 182: 
 183: Two further judgement calls, both flagged for review:
 184: 
 185: 1. **Schema file path.** The story says `server/schemas/rule_bonus_success.schema.js`. Every one of
 186:    the eight existing rule schemas lives at `server/schemas/rules/rule-<family>.schema.js`, and
 187:    `server/routes/rules-engine.js` imports them from there. The new file follows the existing
 188:    convention: `server/schemas/rules/rule-bonus-success.schema.js`.
 189: 
 190: 2. **The "cyclic-reference check" is unimplementable as written, and was deliberately not
 191:    implemented.** The Schema task says "a rule whose `source` is a merit or manoeuvre that is itself
 192:    the `predicate.name` is rejected". The story's own v1 seed is exactly that shape
 193:    (`source: 'Stronger Than You'` gated on `predicate: {kind: 'manoeuvre_present', name: 'Stronger
 194:    Than You'}`), as is AC-1. ADR-001 also explicitly *permits* a rule referencing its own source in a
 195:    condition ("PT references its own rating"); what it forbids is a grant whose **target** is its own
 196:    source. `rule_bonus_success` has no target - the output is successes, not a trait - so no cycle is
 197:    constructible here. Implementing the sentence literally would reject the story's own seed and fail
 198:    its own first acceptance criterion. Instead the route's `postCheck` carries the two structural
 199:    guards that *are* real, both tested at HTTP level:
 200:    - `min_rating` is rejected on any predicate that is not `merit_present` (per the resolved Ask-First
 201:      note: a manoeuvre has no rating).
 202:    - `count_basis: 'rating'` is rejected unless the predicate is `merit_present` (nothing to read a
 203:      rating from otherwise), and `count_basis: 'flat'` requires `flat_amount`.
 204: 
 205:    `server/tests/api-rules-engine.test.js` asserts positively that a self-referencing source/predicate
 206:    pair is **accepted**, so the reasoning is pinned in a test rather than only in prose.
 207: 
 208: ### Design notes
 209: 
 210: - **`combineSuccesses` alongside `resolveSuccesses`.** The story specifies
 211:   `resolveSuccesses(cols, character, rollContext)`; it exists and does exactly that. But the rote path
 212:   has already reduced two pools to one winning **rolled** count by the time the bonus is due, and the
 213:   bonus must be added once, to the winner - so `shared/dice.js` also exports
 214:   `addBonusSuccesses(rolled, character, rollContext)`, and `resolveSuccesses` is a one-line wrapper
 215:   over it. This is what keeps the "never break the best-of-two comparison" boundary honest.
 216: - **The evaluator stays pure and import-free**, like every sibling in `public/js/editor/rule_engine/`.
 217:   It takes the rule docs as an argument; the cache lookup (`getRulesCache().rule_bonus_success`) lives
 218:   in `shared/dice.js`. That is what lets the whole I/O matrix run in vitest with no DB and no browser.
 219: - **`formatSuccessBreakdown` lives in the evaluator module** so the breakdown string has one source of
 220:   truth across every display surface, and is unit-testable without the browser data layer. It returns
 221:   an empty string when no bonus fired, so each surface appends it unconditionally and a normal roll
 222:   renders byte-identically to before.
 223: - **`wTotal === wS` whenever nothing fires**, so the Roll tab's headline count, exceptional-success
 224:   threshold, stake note, history entry and `roll_log` payload are all unchanged on a normal roll.
 225: - **Contested rolls** use the attacker's total against the resistance roll. The resistance roll itself
 226:   stays rolled-only: resolving bonus rules for the *resisting* character would need that character's
 227:   own pool context, which this surface does not have. Noted inline in `roll-v2.js`.
 228: - **feeding-tab's `bestTraitsFor`** was extracted out of `buildPool` because the two ST-confirmed pool
 229:   paths take the pool size straight off the submission and never call `buildPool` - without the
 230:   extraction, a `roll_attr` predicate could not fire on an ST-confirmed feeding pool at all.
 231: - **Persisted feeding rolls** now also carry `rolledSuccesses`, `bonusSuccesses` and
 232:   `successBreakdown`. `downtime_submission.schema.js`'s `rollResult` definition is
 233:   `additionalProperties: true`, so no schema change was needed; rolls persisted before this story have
 234:   no `successBreakdown` and render exactly as they did.
 235: 
 236: ### Findings for review (not fixed here - outside this story's scope)
 237: 
 238: 1. **Players cannot load the rules cache at all, so Stronger Than You will not fire for a player.**
 239:    `/api/rules/aggregate` (and every per-family rules-engine endpoint) is `requireRole('st')`.
 240:    `public/js/app.js:750-758` documents this as an accepted pre-existing degradation ("preloadRules
 241:    403 for a player against the ST-only rules-engine endpoint"), and `applyDerivedMerits` has a
 242:    null-cache guard for it. The new evaluator inherits the same behaviour: cold cache gives
 243:    `bonus === []` and `total === rolled`, which is the story's own defensive AC. But it means the
 244:    mechanic is ST/dev-only in practice until the rules-engine read is opened to players. This is a
 245:    genuine functional gap, it predates this story, and closing it is an auth-boundary decision, not a
 246:    dev-story call.
 247: 2. **`public/js/downtime/roller.js`** is a fourth, structurally different dice implementation (its
 248:    `rollPool` returns a result object, never calls `cntSuc`). It is reached only through
 249:    `public/js/admin/downtime-views.js`, which `public/js/admin.js:45` records as unrouted. Not in the
 250:    story's Code Map, not wired, flagged as a follow-up candidate if that surface is ever revived.
 251: 3. **The seed has not been run.** `node server/scripts/seed-rules-bonus-successes.js --apply` is a
 252:    live-DB write; per this project's standing rule those are run by Angelus, not by the agent. Until
 253:    it runs, `rule_bonus_success` is empty and every roll resolves exactly as it does today.
 254: 4. **No admin editor UI** for the new collection. The story's "Final consequence" explicitly defers
 255:    that ("editor UI ships in a follow-up story; this story is engine + seed only"). A new rule is a
 256:    Mongo insert or a `POST /api/rules/bonus_success` until then.
 257: 
 258: ### Verification run
 259: 
 260: Story-named commands, all green:
 261: 
 262: | Command | Result |
 263: |---|---|
 264: | `cd server && npx vitest run bonus-success` | **40/40 passed** |
 265: | `cd server && npx vitest run rule_engine_grep` | **2/2 passed** |
 266: | `cd server && npx vitest run rule_engine_effective_contract` | **11/11 passed** (6 pre-existing PT + 5 new) |
 267: 
 268: Additional new coverage: `api-rules-engine` **+10** (`rule_bonus_success` CRUD, auth, and each
 269: postCheck rejection), `api-rules-aggregate` **+1** and one existing test widened to 8 categories.
 270: 
 271: Regression sweep (every suite importing a changed module, plus the roll/feeding Playwright specs):
 272: 
 273: - `npx vitest run rule-engine-integration applyDerivedMerits-null-cache-guard gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll
 274:   gdx-8-roll-history rlv-1-combat-tab-quick-roll rlv-6-dice-engine-removed feeding-pool-ambience-vitae
 275:   feeding-grounds-double-free` gives 95 passed, 5 failed. The 5 are all in
 276:   `rule-engine-integration.test.js` and were **confirmed identical at base** via `git stash` A/B
 277:   (5 failed / 2 passed with the changes stashed).
 278: - The 20-suite sweep over every `shared/dice.js` / `load-rules.js` / `roll-v2.js` / `feeding-tab.js`
 279:   importer gives **287 passed, 76 skipped, 9 suite-level failures**, measured **byte-identical at
 280:   base** via `git stash` A/B. All nine fail at import time with "rule docs not found in
 281:   `tm_suite_test`" - they need seeded rule docs in a stale-named test DB, an environment gap, not a
 282:   code defect.
 283: - `npx playwright test tests/issue-1024-roll-v2-anchor-and-again-seg.spec.js
 284:   tests/rlv-2-single-roller-retirement.spec.js` gives **13/13 passed**.
 285: 
 286: ### Visual verification
 287: 
 288: Angelus cannot run the app locally, so the breakdown display was verified with a throwaway Playwright
 289: script (booted `/`, stubbed `Math.random` to a non-exploding success, stubbed
 290: `/api/rules/aggregate` to serve the seed doc, injected a character with the `fighting_picks` entry and
 291: a Strength/Crafts `POOL_INFO`, then called the real `doRoll()`). Live DOM read back:
 292: 
 293:     count:      "8"
 294:     label:      "Exceptional Success"
 295:     verdict:    "Strength 4 + Crafts 3 · 10-again · 7 rolled + 1 (Stronger Than You) = 8 successes"
 296:     pageerrors: []
 297: 
 298: That is the story's specified breakdown shape, rendered by the real code path through the real rules
 299: cache. The script and its artefacts were deleted afterwards (`git status` is clean of them).
 300: 
 301: ### Completion notes
 302: 
 303: All eight Execution tasks are done. Every acceptance criterion has at least one test:
 304: 
 305: | AC | Covered by |
 306: |---|---|
 307: | STY in `fighting_picks` + Strength pool + at least 1 rolled gives `{source, count: 1}` | `bonus-success.test.js` row 1, plus the seed-doc round-trip test |
 308: | Style dots but no pick gives no bonus | row 4 |
 309: | 0 rolled gives `bonus === []`, `total === 0` | rows 2 and 9, plus "never rescue a failure" |
 310: | Dex + Athletics gives no bonus | row 3 |
 311: | ST homebrew rule fires with no code change | "an ST homebrew roll_attr rule fires with no code change" plus the HTTP CRUD tests |
 312: | Empty rules collection gives `total === rolled` | "an empty rules collection leaves the roll untouched", plus null/undefined tolerance |
 313: | Display shows the breakdown; unchanged when empty | `formatSuccessBreakdown` block (4 tests) plus the live-DOM visual verification |
 314: | Vigour-2 regression, `rule_disc_attr` untouched | row 10 plus the "Vigour and Resilience stay in `rule_disc_attr`" boundary guard |
 315: 
 316: The story's "Never" list is additionally pinned by seven source-level boundary guards at the foot of
 317: `bonus-success.test.js` (cntSuc unmodified, `resolveSuccesses` added alongside it, feeding-tab's rote
 318: comparison still rolled-only, roll-v2's rote winner still chosen on rolled successes, the evaluator
 319: absent from `applyDerivedMerits`, Vigour/Resilience untouched, and no reuse of an existing rule
 320: collection).
