   4:  * Without this, integration tests hit `tm_game` (the live DB) and any
   5:  * seed/cleanup leak corrupts production data. Running against `tm_game_test`
   6:  * isolates every insert/update/delete so the worst-case is a polluted
   7:  * throwaway DB you can simply drop.
   8:  *
   9:  * Set BEFORE db.js is imported, because db.js resolves MONGODB_DB at
  10:  * connect time. Vitest's `setupFiles` runs once per worker before test files.
  11:  */
  12: 
  13: import 'dotenv/config';
  14: 
  15: // Hard override — never let a test run touch tm_game, even if a developer
  16: // sets MONGODB_DB=tm_game in their local env. Tests always use tm_game_test.
  17: process.env.MONGODB_DB = 'tm_game_test';
vitest.config.js

